    <DataNode elementId="AT4G26850-MONOMER" textLabel="GDP-L-galactose phosphorylase 1" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="AT4G26850-MONOMER" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="215" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">Two genes, VTC2 and VTC5, in the Arabidopsis genome encode the GDP-L-galactose phosphorylase enzyme for ascorbate biosynthesis. VTC5 is generally expressed at a 100- to 1000-fold lower level than VTC2. VTC5 knockout mutants retain 80% of the wild-type ascorbate level suggesting VTC2 is the major isozyme. Double mutants of VTC2 VTC5 show growth arrest upon germination indicating that both enzymes are necessary for ascorbate biosynthesis.</Comment>
